The point $$$(x_0 - R, y_0)$$$ always lies on the circle because $$$(x_0 - (x_0 - R))^2 + (y_0 - y_0)^2 = R^2$$$ holds for every $$$R$$$: after expanding the parentheses, we get $$$R^2 = R^2$$$.

